    "general": "Take R^a L^a R and L^a R^a R on a line with g(x)=x. Both go from (0,R) to (1,R) in 2a+1 steps with gain sums +/-a^2. Every time-,site-, and direction-dependent translation of the local sheet frame telescopes between the same endpoints. For M>4a^2 the cycle distance of 2a^2 exceeds 2v(2a+1) when a is large enough for any fixed v. There is then no such gauge making the exact whole lift bounded-speed in one tick per base step. This tests the exact transport, not a lower bound on observed coarse probabilities, a separate simulator, or an arbitrarily selected force packet."
